@startuml sequence-diagram-1

' Sheet 1/4 - A4 portrait. See sequence-diagram.puml for the whole diagram.
skinparam dpi 200
scale max 1500*2150

title node-sso-consumer - WSS authentication and realtime delivery of ME\nSheet 1/4: opening the session and the ticket

autonumber

actor "User" as User

participant "Front Application\nBrowser" as Browser
participant "SSO Client\nnode-sso-consumer/client" as Client
participant "Node Application\nnode-sso-consumer" as App
participant "Realtime Bridge\nnode-sso-consumer" as Bridge
participant "x-core\nSSO / Realtime Provider" as XCore


== 1. Creating the SSO client ==

User -> Browser : Opens the application

Browser -> Client : createSsoClient({...})

note right of Client
The SSO instance is created.

It does not hold ME yet.
end note


== 2. Asking for the initial ME ==

Browser -> Client : await sso.connect()

Client -> App : GET /api/auth/session\nHttpOnly cookie

note over Client, App
The browser session is authenticated
by the session cookie.

The cookie carries, among other things,
the encrypted session tokens.
end note

App -> XCore : GET /api/v1/sso/me?accessToken=...\n+ application HMAC authentication

XCore -> XCore : Verifies the application
XCore -> XCore : Verifies the user
XCore -> XCore : Computes profile + permissions

XCore --> App : SsoMe, or 401 if the accessToken has expired

opt accessToken expired
    App -> XCore : PUT /api/v1/sso/consumer/session\n{ refreshToken }
    XCore --> App : new pair\naccessToken + refreshToken
    App -> App : Re-seals the cookie
    App -> XCore : GET /api/v1/sso/me\nwith the new accessToken
    XCore --> App : SsoMe

    note over App, XCore
    The refreshToken is SINGLE USE.

    Without re-sealing the cookie,
    the session dies on the very next call.
    end note
end

App -> XCore : Opens a follow-up WSS for this account\nHMAC handshake + AUTH frame + subscribe

note over App, XCore
A SECOND SOCKET, this one SERVER-side.

SsoLiveAccounts opens ONE per account, on the first
session read, distinct from the browser's own
which is opened on sheet 2.

A plain relay into di.onAccount and di.onSignedOut:
no guard ever reads from it.
end note

App --> Client : SsoMe

Client -> Client : onAccount(me)

Client --> Browser : connect() returns ME


note over Browser, XCore
CAREFUL:

The first ME comes from an HTTP request.

It is NOT yet received
over WebSocket.
end note


== 3. Creating an authenticated WebSocket ticket ==

Client -> App : POST /api/auth/realtime-ticket\nHttpOnly cookie

App -> XCore : GET /api/v1/sso/me\nthe SAME check as in section 2

XCore --> App : SsoMe

note over App, XCore
The ticket route performs NO
local check whatsoever.

It puts the question back to x-core,
rotation included. A session that is over
is refused here, not at the dial.
end note

App -> Bridge : Create a ticket bound\nto the user's accessToken

Bridge -> Bridge : Ticket generation\n32 bytes, 30 seconds, single use

Bridge --> App : ticket

App --> Client : { ticket }


note over Client, Bridge
The browser does NOT receive
the accessToken.

It only receives
a temporary ticket.
end note


note over User, XCore #LightYellow
CONTINUED ON SHEET 2/4:
opening the WebSocket Secure and the double authentication.
end note

@enduml
